domain StableAreaIdentityRepairReview:
  description "Implementation review of initial canonical area identity repair"
problem P1:
  "Restore original area identity and adjacent-hop behavior without changing saved world or external contracts."
premise BOUNDARY:
  |
    Current implementation review covers Accepted ADR0012 deterministic stable
    area/object/effect compiler, ADR0020 D1 one adjacent frozen topology hop,
    ADR0022 canonical placement ownership. It does not accept new persistence,
    external API, asset revision migration, sensory effects or actual provider quality.
evidence E1:
  |
    The prior audited RCA and strengthened before-repair TAP show two areas where
    the declared three-area graph requires three; the first reposition test fails.
    The original label-only initializer remains unchanged for missing-world legacy
    reconstruction. No historical root change or production impact is established.
evidence E2:
  |
    structured-battlefield.ts compiles object/effect scene locations using area names.
    BattlefieldDefinitionV2 permits identical area names but references stable IDs.
    battlefield-creation.ts now consumes the validated definition and constructs
    required instance plus exact initialWorldLayout as one structured creation input.
    This mandatory union rejects omission at compile time. Legacy use of a compiled
    instance is rejected rather than silently reconstructing it by labels.
evidence E3:
  |
    battle-world.ts validates all layout entity/area references and requires a mapping
    for each initial scene entity. It preserves all provided area IDs and placements.
    battle-service.ts passes resolved creation, whose instance is also the existing
    frozen instance used for manifest binding. battle-engine.ts persists only instance.
    ensureBattleWorldState returns saved worlds unchanged and its missing-world path
    continues using the original no-layout initializer.
evidence E4:
  |
    Four core shared files pass71 before the final added reference rejection case.
    Whole shared package now passes419 with all66 files and no skips. Targeted HTTP
    creation/public projection29 cases pass. Strict imported repair path also passes.
    Three-area first hop targets area.2, second targets area.3, and loaded saved world
    retains the same reference. Duplicate named areas retain distinct actor, object
    and area-targeted effect placements. Missing/dangling initial references reject.
evidence E5:
  |
    These are local pure or isolated SQLite tests with injected provider transport,
    not live quality or public acceptance. Existing hidden-object sensory projection,
    whole malformed legacy input matrix, and saved old worlds that already contain
    mismatched IDs are not repaired or certified by this placement correction.
decision D1 based_on P1, BOUNDARY, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5:
  |
    The producing condition on current structured creation is corrected: stable
    definition IDs now cross a mandatory typed creation handoff and validated initial
    world mapping, instead of being regenerated from labels. The strengthened
    regression separately closes the demonstrated detection gap. This conclusion is
    scoped to current new creation and tested graph/duplicate-name fixtures.
decision D2 based_on D1, BOUNDARY, E4, E5:
  |
    INSIDE current obligations are satisfied by source inspection, strict types and
    local tests; final whole-workspace types and fresh source Seal readback still need
    terminal results before formal registration is considered verified. OUTSIDE:
    production/live acceptance and migration of previously saved mismatched worlds
    require their own scope; neither is claimed here. No boundary dispute or new
    architectural decision is introduced by this internal lossless projection.
